<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monckton Commission</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1960</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Monckton Commission was a British advisory commission chaired by Lord Monckton that reviewed the future of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federation-of-rhodesia-and-nyasaland">Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland</a> in 1960. Its report found deep African hostility to the federation and recommended wider African political representation and that member territories should be able to leave. It encouraged the secession of Nyasaland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a>, and the federation was dissolved at the end of 1963.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/monckton-commission.jpg" alt="Monckton Commission" width="300" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Beneaththelandslide at English Wikipedia. · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Federation_of_Rhodesia_and_Nyasaland.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
